  "result": "I found the bug and wrote a plan, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is active. `ExitPlanMode` is disabled in this session, so I can't submit the plan for approval through the tool.\n\n**Root cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py:750-754` returns `bound - dir` for open bounds. `convert` passes `dir=1` when the value is below `min` and `dir=-1` when it is above `max`, so `dir` already points into the range. Subtracting it moves the result further out.\n\nFor example, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` returns `-1` instead of `1`. `max_open` is wrong the same way: it returns `max + 1` instead of `max - 1`.\n\n**Fix:** change `return bound - dir` to `return bound + dir`.\n\n**Tests:** add cases to `tests/test_types.py` for `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"-1\"` \u2192 `1`, and `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"9\"` \u2192 `4`. Then run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nThe full plan is in `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-snuggly-nautilus.md`. Tell me to proceed and I'll make the edit and add the tests.",
